# Patterns and conventions

## File and naming conventions

- API routes: app/server/api/<path>.<method>.ts (method is .get.ts, .post.ts, .patch.ts, .delete.ts)
- Services: app/server/services/<Domain>Service.ts; forecast/* for forecasting domain
- Queues: app/server/queues/*Queue.ts (BullMQ)
- Cron: app/server/cron/*.ts (nuxt-cron)
- Clients: app/server/clients/*Client.ts (Prisma, Redis, NATS, Postmark)
- Zod schemas: app/schema/*.ts
- Prisma: app/prisma/schema.prisma + app/prisma/migrations/* (MySQL provider)
- Tests: colocate under app/server/**/__tests__ or feature-specific folders

## API route implementation checklist

- Validate input with Zod (schema/zod.ts or dedicated schemas) where applicable
- Authenticate early (server/middleware/auth.ts); require admin with server/lib/requireAdmin.ts when needed
- Authorize per-account using accountAccess.ts and accountMembership.ts helpers
- Delegate business logic to server/services/*; keep route handlers thin
- Use withErrorHandler.ts or handleApiError.ts consistently; normalize external errors (e.g., Plaid) via helpers (plaidApiError.ts)
- For long or asynchronous tasks, enqueue via server/queues/* (BullMQ) or expose tasks/* endpoints guarded appropriately
- Add unit tests in app/server/api/__tests__ matching the route path/name

## Services

- Keep pure logic in services; inject dependencies via clients (prismaClient.ts, redisClient.ts)
- Forecast services are heavily tested — run forecast suites before shipping changes (see testing.mdc)
- For Plaid and crypto integrations, prefer dedicated services (PlaidSyncService, PlaidTransactionEnrichmentService, AlchemyService, AssetValueEstimateService)

## Prisma and migrations

- Edit app/prisma/schema.prisma, then create migrations; ensure MySQL decimal precision is appropriate (several migrations convert precision)
- prisma-field-encryption: encrypted fields are annotated in schema.prisma (e.g., User.email, RegisterEntry.description, AccountRegister.plaid*); some fields also have hash annotations for lookup
- Keep microservice/prisma/schema.prisma in sync for models the microservice touches (it’s a subset; do not assume full parity). A governance script exists: scripts/check-prisma-schema-governance.mjs
- Generate client for tests/CI: pnpm --filter dineros-app exec prisma generate

## Security and secrets

- Never commit .env; pre-commit hook blocks it (scripts/check-no-env-committed.sh)
- Do not log secrets; use server/lib/plaidAccessTokenCrypto.ts and hashed columns for lookups
- JWT, RSA, and DB encryption keys are managed via env and K8S secrets; rotate per deployment docs
- Post-restore workflows overwrite or re-encrypt sensitive data for local dev; see docs/post-restore-encryption-plan.md

## Error handling and UX

- Convert internal errors with handleApiError.ts; return user-friendly messages using app/lib/userFriendlyApiError.ts when appropriate
- Server middleware/security headers: app/server/plugins/security-headers.ts

## Testing

- Vitest: unit/integration with TZ=UTC; coverage tasks available
- Playwright: E2E public/authed flows + visual snapshots; Linux baselines can be regenerated in CI (workflow: e2e-update-staging-snapshots.yml)
- Forecast engine has a dedicated test runner and granular suites; run test:forecast:all before changes that affect balances, interest, or schedules

## UI/UX conventions

- Components in components/ and feature-heavy pages under pages/
- State via Pinia (stores/*)
- Tailwind CSS used (assets/css/main.css)

## Safe change recipes

- Add a new API endpoint:
  1) Create app/server/api/<path>.<method>.ts
  2) Validate input with Zod; authz with account* helpers
  3) Delegate to a service; add tests under server/api/__tests__
  4) If background work, add a queue and/or cron thoughtfully
- Modify Prisma schema:
  1) Update app/prisma/schema.prisma
  2) Add a migration (and parallel update in microservice if needed)
  3) Regenerate Prisma client, run tests
  4) Review encryption annotations and seed updates if necessary
- Update forecast logic:
  1) Edit forecast services in server/services/forecast/*
  2) Run unit/integration/regression suites; ensure no balance continuity regressions

## Branching, commits, CI gates

- Branch names: short descriptive (see CONTRIBUTING.md)
- Run pnpm lint and pnpm test before pushing
- CI: PRs run lint/test/CodeQL and (for in-repo branches) build + staging deploy; main deploys to production
